<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Counting digital security codes without repetition</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> A security code uses \({@plen1@}\) different digits chosen from \(0\)–\(9\), with no digit repeated. How many different codes are possible?</p>
<p>Number of codes = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><b>(b)</b> A different code uses \({@plen2@}\) different letters chosen from the \(26\) letters of the alphabet, with no letter repeated. How many different codes are possible?</p>
<p>Number of codes = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>Because the order of characters in a security code matters and no character may be repeated, use the permutation formula:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_nP_r = \frac{n!}{(n - r)!}\)</p>

<p><b>Part (a): \({@plen1@}\)-digit code from \(10\) digits (\(0\)–\(9\))</b><br>
Substitute \(n = 10\) and \(r = {@plen1@}\), expand \(10!\) down to \({@rem1@}!\), and cancel \({@rem1@}!\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_{10}P_{{@plen1@}} = \frac{10!}{(10 - {@plen1@})!} = \frac{10!}{{@rem1@}!} = \frac{{@num1_factors@} \times {@rem1@}!}{{@rem1@}!} = {@num1_factors@} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of digit codes} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part (b): \({@plen2@}\)-letter code from \(26\) letters</b><br>
Substitute \(n = 26\) and \(r = {@plen2@}\), expand \(26!\) down to \({@rem2@}!\), and cancel \({@rem2@}!\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_{26}P_{{@plen2@}} = \frac{26!}{(26 - {@plen2@})!} = \frac{26!}{{@rem2@}!} = \frac{{@num2_factors@} \times {@rem2@}!}{{@rem2@}!} = {@num2_factors@} = {@ta2@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of letter codes} = {@ta2@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
